[FINAL-TEXT] **Phase 5 — diagnosis confirmed.** The running config shows a completely bare FRR instance: no `router ospf` block, no `network` statements, no routing whatsoever. This is direct, unambiguous evidence.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch_server_access
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** OSPF routing configuration on `switch_server_access` — the FRR router that serves as gateway (10.200.0.1) for all data-centre hosts (web servers and DNS server on the 10.200.0.0/24 subnet).

**Mechanism:** `switch_server_access` has a completely unconfigured FRR instance — its `show running-config` output contains no `router ospf` block and no `network` statements whatsoever. Because it never sends or accepts OSPF Hello packets, it is invisible to the rest of the routing domain. Two consequences flow from this: (1) the 10.200.0.0/24 prefix is never originated into OSPF, so every other router — including `switch_dist_1_1` and `switch_dist_2_1` — has no route to the server subnet and their gateways correctly return "Destination Net Unreachable" to user hosts; (2) `switch_server_access` itself has learned zero OSPF routes, so it cannot forward packets toward user subnets (10.1.1.0/24, 10.2.1.0/24) and returns "Destination Net Unreachable" to servers. The secondary observable effect is that `router_core_3`'s eth2 (172.16.0.10/31 — its uplink to `switch_server_access`) shows 0 neighbors and 0 adjacencies, because no peer ever replies to its OSPF Hellos.

**Localization:** `switch_server_access` — single device, all interfaces affected.

**Root cause:** OSPF is entirely absent from the FRR configuration on `switch_server_access`; no routing protocol participates, so the server segment is a routing black hole in both directions.

**Fix:** Add OSPF configuration to `switch_server_access`: create a `router ospf` block and add `network 172.16.0.10/31 area 0.0.0.0` (uplink to router_core_3) and `network 10.200.0.0/24 area 0.0.0.0` (or the appropriate stub area), then reload FRR to form the missing adjacency with router_core_3 and advertise the server subnet.
=== END ===